{
  "format": "supersilvia-workspace",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Reaction-diffusion",
  "kind": "video",
  "blurb": "Blur and sharpen fed back until noise grows into a Turing pattern",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Feed a frame back through a Blur and then a hard Sharpen and the two fight: the blur spreads every spot and the sharpen pushes it back into an edge, so a little noise grows into winding stripes, the way chemicals pattern a fish's skin. The two Zooms read the loop three times bigger, which sets the stripes' width. Turn the Sharpen's Amount, or the first Zoom."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
